+# RGB HTLC wire contract, version 1
+
+Shared with the swap SDK. Captured from maker revision
+`49c6ce2e9554eea0d819fd3bbd267af6db45b1c0` through the actual axum router with
+isolated PostgreSQL, mock chain/node/wallet state and the real rgb-lib recipient
+encoder. rgb-lib is pinned to `96f039d975cf2a83712c3c0a90e703621d445425`, resolving
+rgb-invoicing `0.11.1-rc.11`. The test contract was not issued; no RGB proofs or
+live wallet transfers are claimed. Auth tokens and invoices belong to disposable
+mock swaps. The claim prevout is synthetic.
+
+Run the four database-free compatibility tests:
+
+```sh
+cargo test -p maker-api --test rgb_wire_contract --locked
+```
+
+To recapture deliberately, use a disposable PostgreSQL instance:
+
+```sh
+TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:rgb-wire-test@127.0.0.1:15433/postgres \
+RGB_WIRE_FIXTURE_OUTPUT="$PWD/tests/fixtures/rgb-v1" \
+cargo test -p maker-api --test rgb_wire_capture -- --ignored --nocapture
+```
+
+Copy both JSON files into the SDK's `tests/fixtures/rgb-v1/` and run its
+`cargo test --test rgb_contract` too. IDs, blinding and invoice timestamps vary
+on capture; CI consumes one frozen capture. Its pair limits use input units,
+miner fees use output units, and rates convert between the two. The RGB contract
+has 6 decimals and the internal quote card has 8.
